* text=auto eol=lf

*.blade.php diff=html
*.css diff=css
*.html diff=html
*.md diff=markdown
*.php diff=php

/.github export-ignore
CHANGELOG.md export-ignore
.styleci.yml export-ignore

# ── Built frontend assets: use 'theirs' merge driver ─────────────────────────
# These files are regenerated by `npm run build` — hash-based filenames change
# on every build. The server never edits them locally. On `git pull`, we always
# want the incoming GitHub version. The 'incoming' driver (configured by
# deploy.sh) resolves conflicts by taking the remote/incoming side, so
# `git pull` NEVER produces <<< conflict markers in these files.
public/index.html merge=incoming
public/index.html.br merge=binary
public/index.html.gz merge=binary
public/assets/* merge=incoming
public/assets/*.br merge=binary
public/assets/*.gz merge=binary
